  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "**Problem description:**\nThe EditorOnly tagged objects get removed from the hierarchy when building. ✅\nThe related assets to these GOs get included in the build. ❌\n**Personal scenario & replication steps:**\nI use multiple copies of my VRC avatar mesh *(no VRC Avatar scripts attached)* to test player lightning in my editor. They're all tagged EditorOnly and they get removed in the hierarchy during built. However all the textures, shaders, etc do get included in the build, thus bloating the world size, making the use of the EditorOnly tag semi-useless.\n**Possible solution:**\nSimply deactivating the Game Objects in the hierarchy before build fixes this issue.\nI tried creating a `IPreprocessBuildWithReport` script that runs before build to do just that, but I think the VRCSDK stops it from doing its thing as it suddenly loses all its references to `UnityEditor.Build` & `UnityEditor.Build.Reporting` when I press Build & Test.\n**Current workaround:**\nManually deactivating EditorOnly tagged GOs in hierarchy before build.\n\n\n**TL;DR**\nWhen all GameObjects with the EditorOnly tag get destroyed, their assets should not be included in the build.",
